From: Vili Kohonen <vili.kohonen@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Every entrypoint forwards --key=value flags to the training
 config, and unknown keys fail before training

fire calls the entrypoint first and rejects leftover flags afterwards (exit 2), so an
entrypoint without **kwargs trains the full run with the flag ignored and then kills the
pod script on the way out. Now each run_* forwards **kwargs to main_run_rl, which rejects
any key GRPOConfig does not declare (pydantic would otherwise ignore it silently).
